  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the labor law, in relation to the calculation of weekly\nemployment insurance benefits for certain workers; to amend a chapter of the\nlaws of 2021 amending the labor law relating to the calculation of weekly\nemployment insurance benefits for workers who are partially unemployed, as\nproposed in legislative bills numbers S. 1042-A and A. 2355-A, in relation to\nthe effectiveness thereof; and to repeal certain provisions of the labor law\nrelating thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S7148",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7148-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§524, 581, 591, 591-a, 596, 599 & 601, rpld §590 sub 5 ¶(d), Lab L; add §§31 & 32, amd §31, Chap of 2021 (as proposed in S.1042-A & A.2355-A)",
    "lawSection": "Labor Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7148\n\nSPONSOR: RAMOS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the labor law, in relation to the calculation of weekly\nemployment insurance benefits for certain workers; to amend a chapter of\nthe laws of 2021 amending the labor law relating to the calculation of\nweekly employment insurance benefits for workers who are partially unem-\nployed, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 1042-A and A.\n2355-A, in relation to the effectiveness thereof; and to repeal certain\nprovisions of the labor law relating thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of the bill is to make technical and substantive amendments\nto the chapter of the laws of 2021 as proposed in legislative bills\nnumbers S.1042-A and A.2355-A.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill amends various sections of a chapter of the laws of 2021 as\nproposed in legislative bills numbers S. 1042-A and A. 2355-A.  Sections\n1 to 13 institute technical conforming changes to Article 18 of the\nLabor Law.\n\nSection 14 of the bill establishes a temporary partial unemployment\nprogram intended to be in effect until the permanent partial unemploy-\nment program established in the underlying bill becomes effective.\n\nSection 15 of the bill amends the effective date of the underlying chap-\nter.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:  The chapter of the laws of 2021 as proposed in legis-\nlative bills numbers S.1042-A and A.2355-A replaces the current system\nfor determining eligibility for partial unemployment insurance benefits\nwith a system that is based on the claimant's weekly earnings rather\nthan the number of days the claimant worked during the week. The system\nof calculating partial unemployment insurance benefits in an earnings-\nbased model disregards a portion of part-time earnings before reducing\nbenefits by one dollar for each dollar of earnings up to the full weekly\nbenefit amount. Prior law imposed a 25-percent reduction to a claimant's\nfull benefit for any work performed on a single day, which failed to\nprovide an adequate level of income security for workers experiencing\nreductions in their usual hours and earnings and at the same time,\ncreated perverse incentives that may discourage claimants from returning\nto part-time work, particularly for three days or more.\n\nThis bill amends the underlying chapter by making conforming technical\nchanges in the unemployment insurance law, modifying the effective date\nto allow sufficient time for modernization of the unemployment insurance\nsystem, and establishing a temporary hours-based partial unemployment\nprogram to reform the partial unemployment system in a manner that can\nbe put in effect soon as thirty days after enactment.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNot yet determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided that sections one\nthrough fourteen of this act shall take effect on the same date and in\nthe same manner as a chapter of the laws of 2021 amending the labor law\nrelating to the calculation of weekly employment insurance benefits for\nworkers who are partially unemployed, as proposed in legislative bills\nnumbers S. 1042-A and A. 2355-A, takes effect; provided, however, that\nthe amendments to subdivision 1 of section 591 of the labor law made by\nsection four of this act shall be subject to the expiration and rever-\nsion of such subdivision pursuant to section 10 of chapter 413 of the\nlaws of 2003, as amended, when upon such date the provisions of section\nfive of this act shall take effect; and provided, further, that the\namendments to section 591-a of the labor law made by sections eight and\nnine of this act shall not affect the expiration and repeal of such\nsection and shall expire and be deemed repealed therewith.\n",
